\title{An option order stated as an implied volatility, priced with the Black-76 model and re-priced as the underlying and time move}
\description{
This is the Atlas's G7, an order such as "buy this call at 12.5 volatility". UBI works out the premium from the volatility, the option's strike, expiry and type, the watched instrument's last price as the forward, grown by \code{interest_rate} to expiry unless it is a future, and the time to 15:30 on the expiry date, in years of 365 days. It follows the watched instrument through the same step and throttle as an \code{UnderlyingPegOrder}. The template must be a \code{limit} order, and its \code{price} is the worst it accepts, the most a buy pays or the least a sell takes; the model's premium is used whenever it is better. Changing the order's price yourself makes it take the volatility your price implies and carry on at that. \code{lowest_price} and \code{highest_price} never push the order past that worst price, and an option that has already expired is refused with HTTP 400.

The order template's attributes are described on \code{SyntheticOrder}.
}
